{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And your issue, etc.</b> If you beget more, they shall not be counted among my sons, but shall be included within the tribes of Ephraim and Manasseh, and they shall have no name among the tribes regarding inheritance. And even though the land was apportioned by the count of their persons, as it is written ״לָרַב תַּרְבֶּה נַחֲלָתוֹ״ (Numbers 26), and each and every man took equally apart from the firstborns — nonetheless only these were called tribes (to cast the lot of the land by the count of the names of the tribes, and a prince for each and every tribe, and banners for this one and for that one)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:55.031208955Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}